# Observability Lab: Splunk Search & New Relic APM Performance Auditing

## 1\. Audit Overview & Objectives

The audit investigates checkout performance degradation by correlating Splunk web access logs with New Relic Browser monitoring and New Relic APM transaction traces.

Splunk was used to identify HTTP 5xx failures and response times for the affected checkout endpoint. New Relic Browser timing was used to determine whether the user\-facing delay originated from frontend processing or backend response time. New Relic APM was then used to isolate the backend component contributing most of the transaction latency.

The investigation showed that /checkout/payment experienced multiple HTTP 502/504 failures with response times close to 5 seconds. New Relic identified the external PaymentGatewayClient.charge operation as the primary backend bottleneck.

