## 3\. New Relic Browser Timing Breakdown

The total checkout page load time was **6.84 seconds (6840 ms)**.

| Page Load Phase | Duration (ms) | Percentage of Total Page Load (%) | Operational Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **DNS Lookup** | 18 | 0.26% | Time required to resolve the website hostname |
| **TCP & SSL Handshake** | 42 | 0.61% | Time required to establish the network connection and TLS session |
| **Backend Duration (TTFB)** | 5120 | 74.85% | Time the browser waited for the server/backend response |
| **DOM Processing** | 1120 | 16.37% | Time spent processing the HTML and constructing the DOM |
| **Page Rendering** | 540 | 7.89% | Time spent rendering the page in the browser |
| **Total Page Load Time** | 6840 | 100% | Complete observed checkout page\-load duration |

The backend TTFB of **5120 ms** represented approximately **74.85%** of the complete page\-load time. Therefore, the majority of the user\-facing delay originated from the server\-side processing rather than DNS, connection establishment or frontend rendering.

The New Relic Browser Apdex score was **0.41**, further indicating significant degradation in the checkout user experience.

