## 4\. New Relic APM Transaction Trace Breakdown

Transaction:

WebTransaction/Custom/Checkout/SubmitOrder

Total transaction duration: **5120 ms**

| Segment Name | Total Duration (ms) | Exclusive Duration (ms) | Percentage Contribution (%) |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Application: CheckoutController.submit | 5120 | 25 | 0.49% |
| External: PaymentGatewayClient.charge | 5080 | 5080 | 99.22% |
| Database: Postgres OrderRepository.save | 15 | 15 | 0.29% |

The CheckoutController.submit segment represents the overall application transaction, but only **25 ms** was exclusive application\-processing time.

The external PaymentGatewayClient.charge call consumed **5080 ms**, representing **99.22%** of the complete backend transaction.

The PostgreSQL save operation took only **15 ms**, indicating that the database was not the primary bottleneck in this incident.

